            <ArticleTitle>Effects of long-term treatment with metiamide.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>134-43</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Metiamide was given to patients with peptic ulcer or oesophagitis in a pilot study to establish the therapeutic value of the drug. Administration of metiamide resulted in relief of pain within a week in the majority of patients. Healing of duodenal and gastric ulcers was observed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
